    },
    "message": "Check support travel on the shared generated Scenario\n\nThese tests took the small replay fixture and hand-added a floor plan\nwithout facility awareness, a combination the UI never makes. They now\nuse the shared generated Scenario (#88): the support worker is\nstaff_001 in the staff area, the first leg is route_sleeping_corridor,\nand a staff absence is passed as an operational condition.\n\nGenerated floor plans have one route per area, so the reroute test adds\na second, slower route through the same doors and registers it on\nthose doors. Generated people also carry minute-by-minute psychological\nstate, so the walk-to-the-worker test now runs the tick order with the\nTickEngine and moves to tests/integration/test_staff_support_travel.py.\nThe legacy continuity receipt test needs no Scenario and stays in this\nfile, now tests/unit/domain/test_common_operations.py.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
